<div class="page-header">
  <h1 class="page-title">Cookie policy</h1>
</div>

<div class="page-prose">
  <p>
    This is a static site: it has no server of its own, it stores nothing about you and it
    <strong>sets no cookies by itself</strong>. We use no analytics either, so we collect no
    statistics about your visit and do not know which pages you read.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two pages do embed third-party content, and those services may set their own cookies when you
    load the page containing them:
  </p>

  <ul class="page-list">
    <li><a href="/en/about-us">The project</a> includes a video hosted on <strong>YouTube</strong> (Google).</li>
    <li><a href="/en/the-books">The books</a> includes the chapter presentations hosted on <strong>Speakerdeck</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Those cookies are set by those services, not by us, and are governed by their own policies. If
    you would rather avoid them, you can block third-party cookies in your browser settings: the
    rest of the site works exactly the same.
  </p>
</div>
